{title: 151 - Jesus Walked This Lonesome Valley}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #151 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 151}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Jesus walked this lonesome valley;
[F/A]He had to walk it [Am]by Himself.
[C7/Bb]O [Am]nobody [Dm/A]else [Am]could walk it [F]for Him.
[Dm]He had [Am]to walk [Gm]it by Himself.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]I must go and stand my trial.
[F/A]I have to stand it [Am]by myself.
[C7/Bb]O [Am]nobody [Dm/A]else [Am]could stand it [F]for me.
[Dm]I have [Am]to stand [Gm]it by myself.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]Jesus walked this lonesome valley;
[F/A]He had to walk it [Am]by Himself.
[C7/Bb]O [Am]nobody [Dm/A]else [Am]could walk it [F]for Him.
[Dm]He had [Am]to walk [Gm]it by Himself.
{end_of_verse}
